work and lack of feedback handling evidence. Perhaps propose a mitigation plan. Or we could shift to Candidate C because of crew cooperation (concern for others) and quick decision making, but his communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are concerns. Probably still B.\n\nThus as Anna, we can say we still recommend B, but we need to address feedback handling. Maybe ask for concrete example of B's feedback handling from other panel members? But we have no tool call now; we could ask but we need to keep one focused contribution. Could ask a question to Agent 2 or 3 via tool, but we are in public turn. We could ask via tool to get more info on B's feedback handling. However we can also just state that we still recommend B, but we need to ensure crew cooperation is addressed.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I still recommend Candidate B, because his reliability, stress resilience, technical competence outweigh the interpersonal concerns, and the other candidates have more serious deficits.\" Also note that we still lack evidence on feedback handling, but we can mitigate.\n\nThen METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
